# Security and Best Practices Rules

## Security Guidelines

- Validate all user inputs before processing
- Follow principle of least privilege
- Don't expose sensitive data in logs or error messages
- Use proper sanitization for file operations
- Avoid eval() and similar dangerous functions

## Input Validation

- Always validate user input from commands and inputs
- Sanitize file paths and URIs
- Validate JSON before parsing
- Check file permissions before operations
- Handle edge cases gracefully

## Error Handling

- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Log errors appropriately without exposing sensitive data
- Handle async operations errors properly
- Don't expose internal implementation details
- Use proper error boundaries

## VSCode Extension Security

- Request only necessary permissions in package.json
- Validate workspace paths and file operations
- Handle extension activation errors gracefully
- Use secure defaults for configurations
- Follow VSCode security guidelines

## Code Security

- Avoid using innerHTML with user content
- Validate external dependencies
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Avoid dangerous eval-like operations
- Keep dependencies updated

